Solving Circular Dependency

Suppose

java
@Service
public class AService {

    @Autowired
    private BService b;

}


java
@Service
public class BService {

    @Autowired
    private AService a;

}


Spring


Create A

Needs B

Create B

Needs A

Already creating A

↓

Circular dependency


Application fails.

---

Solution

java
@Service
public class BService {

    @Autowired
    @Lazy
    private AService a;

}


Now Spring injects proxy.


A

↓

B

↓

Proxy(A)

↓

Application Starts


